<section class="pack-types" aria-labelledby="packs-heading">
  <div class="container">
    <h1 id="packs-heading">What Are Booster Packs?</h1>

    <div class="tldr-box">
      <h2>TL;DR</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Single booster pack</strong> — 10 cards, cheapest way to open something. ~$4–5 each.</li>
        <li><strong>Booster bundle</strong> — 6 packs in a box. Convenient, no extras. ~$25–30.</li>
        <li><strong>Elite Trainer Box (ETB)</strong> — 9 packs + sleeves + dice + a storage box. Great starter. ~$40–50.</li>
        <li><strong>Booster box</strong> — 36 packs. For serious collectors. ~$130–150.</li>
        <li><strong>Starter deck</strong> — A ready-to-play 60-card deck. For kids who want to learn the game. ~$12–15.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
      <div class="pack-type-card" id="{{ block.settings.anchor }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
        <div class="pack-type-image">
          {%- if block.settings.image -%}
            <img
              src="{{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 400 }}"
              alt="{{ block.settings.title }}"
              width="400"
              height="auto"
              loading="lazy"
            >
          {%- else -%}
            <div class="pack-type-placeholder">
              <p>Upload a photo of this product type in the theme editor.</p>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if block.settings.image_attribution -%}
            <p class="image-attribution">{{ block.settings.image_attribution }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
        <div class="pack-type-info">
          <h2>{{ block.settings.title }}</h2>
          <p class="pack-type-price">{{ block.settings.price_range }}</p>
          <div class="rte">{{ block.settings.description }}</div>
          <div class="pack-type-when">
            <strong>When to buy this:</strong>
            <p>{{ block.settings.when_to_buy }}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Pack Types Guide",
  "class": "section-pack-types",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "pack_type",
      "name": "Pack Type",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "title",
          "label": "Product type name",
          "default": "Single Booster Pack"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "anchor",
          "label": "Anchor ID (for linking)",
          "default": "single-pack"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "price_range",
          "label": "Typical price range",
          "default": "~$4–5 each"
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "description",
          "label": "Description",
          "default": "<p>A single booster pack contains 10 cards from the current set. One of those cards is guaranteed to be a 'rare' or better, but 'rare' in Pokémon doesn't always mean valuable — it just means it's less common in the set.</p><p>This is the simplest, cheapest way for a kid to open something and see what they get. Think of it like a surprise bag.</p>"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "when_to_buy",
          "label": "When to buy this",
          "default": "When you want a small, inexpensive surprise. Great for rewards, stocking stuffers, or just letting a kid open something fun."
        },
        {
          "type": "image_picker",
          "id": "image",
          "label": "Product photo"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "image_attribution",
          "label": "Image attribution (if needed)",
          "default": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Pack Types Guide",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "pack_type",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Single Booster Pack",
            "anchor": "single-pack",
            "price_range": "~$4–5 each",
            "description": "<p>A single booster pack contains 10 cards from the current set. One of those cards is guaranteed to be a 'rare' or better, but 'rare' in Pokémon doesn't always mean valuable — it just means it's less common in the set.</p><p>This is the simplest, cheapest way for a kid to open something and see what they get. Think of it like a surprise bag.</p>",
            "when_to_buy": "When you want a small, inexpensive surprise. Great for rewards, stocking stuffers, or just letting a kid open something fun."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "pack_type",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Booster Bundle",
            "anchor": "booster-bundle",
            "price_range": "~$25–30",
            "description": "<p>A booster bundle is a box containing 6 booster packs. No extra supplies — just packs. It's a convenient way to buy several packs at once without paying single-pack markup.</p>",
            "when_to_buy": "When your child wants to open several packs in one sitting. Good for a birthday gift or a weekend activity."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "pack_type",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Elite Trainer Box (ETB)",
            "anchor": "etb",
            "price_range": "~$40–50",
            "description": "<p>An Elite Trainer Box (commonly called an ETB) includes 9 booster packs, 65 card sleeves, energy cards, dice, condition markers, and a sturdy box that doubles as storage. It's designed as an all-in-one starter product.</p><p>This is often the best first purchase for a new collector because it comes with everything they need to start.</p>",
            "when_to_buy": "When your child is just starting out and you want one box that covers packs + basic supplies. A popular gift choice."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "pack_type",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Booster Box",
            "anchor": "booster-box",
            "price_range": "~$130–150",
            "description": "<p>A booster box contains 36 booster packs from a single set. It's the most cost-effective way to open a large number of packs. Often bought by experienced collectors who want broad coverage of a set.</p><p>Important: Even with 36 packs, there's no guarantee of pulling any specific card. The fun is in the variety, not in chasing one card.</p>",
            "when_to_buy": "For experienced collectors who want lots of packs. Not recommended as a first purchase — start smaller to see if they enjoy it before going bigger."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "pack_type",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Build & Battle / Starter Deck",
            "anchor": "starter-deck",
            "price_range": "~$12–15",
            "description": "<p>A starter deck (or Build & Battle kit) is a pre-made 60-card deck that's ready to play right out of the box. It comes with instructions for learning the Pokémon Trading Card Game.</p><p>If your child wants to actually play the game (not just collect), this is where to start. It teaches the rules step by step.</p>",
            "when_to_buy": "When your child wants to learn how to play the card game, not just collect. Also a great affordable gift."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
